# Data conversion between gigabyte and kibibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gigabyte and kibibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GB to 976562.50KiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GB yields 1464843.750KiB; backward, converting 1KiB to 0.0000GB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 0.0000GB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GB
print(forward_whole->to(KiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(forward_fractional->to(KiB))
backward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(backward_whole->to(GB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(backward_fractional->to(GB))

<<< stdout
976562.50KiB
1464843.750KiB
0.0000GB
0.0000GB

<<< stderr
